  "releaseNotes": "Adds a build-time expression compile seam: IFlowExpressionEngine.Compile<T> (default-implemented, non-breaking) returns an IFlowCompiledExpression<T> so expressions parse once at build time instead of per message. ExpressionFlowPredicate now compiles once, a new ExpressionFlowMapper mirrors it for mapping, and the engine's own conditional links compile once. Event channels now use the non-lossy fanout source instead of a lossy broadcast block.",
